<title>DUBAI: Saudi Arabia's Q2 M3 grows 2.6 percent qtr on qtr.</title>
<headline>Saudi Arabia's Q2 M3 grows 2.6 percent qtr on qtr.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's broadly defined M3 money supply rose 2.6 percent in the second quarter of 1996 over the previous quarter, Saudi Arabian Monetary Agency (SAMA) figures show.</p>
<p>Annual average M3 in 1995 grew 3.5 percent after shrinking 1.5 percent in 1994.</p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over three months)</p>
<p>			 Q2 1996		   Q1 1996 M3</p>
<p>			 +2.6			+2.2 M2</p>
<p>			 +3.6			+2.4 M1</p>
<p>			 +4.3			+2.6</p>
<p>Monetary aggregates (riyal millions)</p>
<p>		     Q2 1996		   Q1 1996 M3</p>
<p>		     249,559.7		 243,197.0 M2</p>
<p>		     195,137.9		 188,354.4 M1</p>
<p>		     133,019.5		 127,528.0</p>
</text>
